<title>GERMANY: Veba to create 15,000 jobs in coming years.</title>
<headline>Veba to create 15,000 jobs in coming years.</headline>
<dateline>BONN 1996-11-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>German diversified group Veba AG said it plans to create 15,000 jobs in the coming years, mainly in its telecommunications division in which it plans to add 10,000 jobs.</p>
<p>Veba chief executive Ulrich Hartmann told newspaper Handelsblatt in an interview that the group would start adding jobs next year.</p>
<p>He also said that Deutsche Telekom AG, the telecommunications giant floated on the stock market last week, would remain dominant in its relevant sectors for decades to come.</p>
<p>&quot;But although we are like David facing this Goliath, we are not afraid of Deutsche Telekom,&quot; Hartmann said.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
